{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3068","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3068","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3068\",\"parent_revision\":\"431ecc39bf41c1aac9b0423aceef67bdc316bdeec1ed74f0c445f121e3cb2796\",\"root_revision\":\"431ecc39bf41c1aac9b0423aceef67bdc316bdeec1ed74f0c445f121e3cb2796\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`'s `description`/`author` derive from `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` at sync time (or the drift is otherwise closed).\\n- [ ] A workflow-level test proves editing the Claude manifest's `description` and re-running sync updates the Codex manifest's `longDescription`/`shortDescription`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a maintainer, I want `sync_codex_plugin_manifests.py` to derive each Codex manifest's `description`/`author` from the Claude source manifest (`.claude-plugin/plugin.json`) instead of reading them from the Codex manifest itself, so a future edit to a plugin's Claude description propagates automatically instead of requiring a second hand-edit.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSurfaced while fixing PR #2787 deferred findings #1/#8/#10/#11 (issue #3049) \u2014 `sync_manifest()` currently reads `description`/`author` from `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` itself, which the sync script also writes, so the two stay in sync only by convention at plugin-creation time, not by the sync logic. Out of that fix's assigned scope.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d740129a32c291fccb63615797d040f4cbd795d5c1ea1bc4d93e86bbab384dae\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvcSIQ\"}"}